          amount = _base_amount * mult
          speed_scale = _base_speed_scale * mult
          restart()

  - [1mNormal values come from the scene.[0m In [38;5;153m_ready()[39m the script saves the spark count
    and speed the node starts with. Each burst works from those saved values, so a
    crit followed by a normal strike goes back to normal instead of doubling again.
  - [1mSpeed-up method:[0m I made the sparks faster with [38;5;153mspeed_scale[39m. That also makes them
    burn out in half the time. If you'd rather they travel faster but last just as
    long, I can raise their launch velocity instead.
  - [1mEffect on [38;5;153mcool_down()[39m:[0m it still sets the count to 8, but the next burst now
    resets the count to the scene's starting value. If cool-down is meant to keep
    later strikes smaller, that's worth checking.
  - [1mHooking it up:[0m nothing in the project calls [38;5;153mburst()[39m yet, so the strike code needs
    to call [38;5;153mburst(true)[39m on a crit.

